    "created_at": "2025-04-22T13:07:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-22T13:07:18Z",
    "body": "@EdgarChen @rniwa @domenic @mfreed7 it seems the behavior that everyone copied from Chromium is such that if `anchor` is not given, we use the form-associated custom element as validation anchor. However, if you explicitly use the form-associated custom element as validation anchor, that ends up throwing. This is also tested by WPT:\n```\n  assert_throws_dom('NotFoundError', () => {\n    control.i.setValidity(flags, m, control);\n  }, 'Self');\n```\nI have a patch that makes the specification match exactly this (#11247), but I wonder if we should change step 7 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-elementinternals-setvalidity to instead check for a \"shadow-including inclusive descendant\" instead of a \"shadow-including descendant\".\n\nI could see an argument that forbidding the fallback behavior from being specified explicitly is by design, but it seems a bit curious.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2821275733/reactions",
